Workstream ID: sitewide-visual-polish
Title: Refine every CareerOS page into a polished minimal interface
Status: DONE
Milestone: Deliver research-led visual refinement and its separately authorized publication
Dependencies: calm-interface, omscs-specializations
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/CareerOS/issues/18
Purpose: Retain the accepted content reduction while restoring strong visual
  hierarchy, coherent spacing, aligned controls, clear affordances and an
  attractive interface throughout the existing product. Research primary
  usability/design-system/accessibility guidance before applying it. Check
  actual internal routes, not just the previously reported screenshots.

Tasks:
  [x] Review primary usability/design-system sources and record transfer limits.
  [x] Inventory first-party route patterns and data-driven internal URLs.
  [x] Capture and inspect the actual desktop/tablet/phone baseline safely.
  [x] Refine shared heading/action/card/form/disclosure layout and visual rhythm.
  [x] Correct page-specific empty, populated, detail and overlay rough edges.
  [x] Preserve minimal copy, both themes, readable type and real data semantics.
  [x] Audit internal URL layouts and inspect all primary page families visually.
  [x] Add targeted layout regressions and run appropriate existing suites.
  [x] Record exact source/coverage, focused documentation and same-identity tracking.
  [x] Preserve previews and the initial local-only handoff before separate publication approval.

Acceptance criteria:
  The content-reduction direction remains intact. Do not restore explanatory
    essays, add decorative prose or hide essential records/warnings to make
    a layout simpler. Intentional study material remains complete.
  First-party routes and data-driven destinations have an explicit inventory.
    Record actual checked URLs/viewports/states and manual visual-review scope;
    do not call a few representative screenshots an exhaustive URL audit.
  Shared headings, action groups, cards, rows, disclosures and forms use
    consistent alignment, grouping and spacing. Primary actions are clear,
    supporting actions remain discoverable and text/icon controls fit.
  Desktop, tablet and narrow layouts reflow without clipped text/buttons,
    unintended overlap or whole-document horizontal scrolling. Deliberate
    diagram/table scrolling remains local and accessible.
  Retain DeepSeaFoam/Harbor Daylight, the established type scale, semantic
    mission/status colors, real 3D graph and sun/moon theme behavior. Visual
    polish is not permission to shrink type or invent progress.
  Context help, disclosures, native dialogs, focus indicators, errors and
    meaningful disabled states remain usable by keyboard and touch. Distinguish
    accessibility criteria from design recommendations and actual qualification.
  Preserve IDs, course/grade rules, source workbooks, frozen roadmap editions,
    approved README illustrations, user data, backups and manual journal semantics.
  All browser checks use disposable synthetic/public-starter contexts, never
    the owner's actual profile. Preserve existing user previews and stop only
    identified temporary helpers; no unrelated process or browser disruption.
  Research is applied critically, not copied as a foreign visual identity.
    Keep findings, project choices, observed defects and unverified assumptions
    separate. No private inputs are sent to research services or public tracking.
  Keep technical verification, human visual approval and publication separate.
    Publication does not follow from the initial local review request alone.
    A later explicit owner deployment decision is separate; private image/
    report upload and human aesthetic approval are not inferred.

